Restore warning topics still referenced by odls_base_bind.c in PRRTE 4.1.0.
Without them, pmix_show_help_vstring returns NULL and write_help_msg calls
strlen(NULL) when memory binding is denied, for example by Docker seccomp.
The upstream fork/exec refactor also restores these topics:
https://github.com/openpmix/prrte/commit/f24b3f384ac07737af922b045fedaee4e6063c74

--- a/src/mca/odls/pdefault/help-prte-odls-default.txt
+++ b/src/mca/odls/pdefault/help-prte-odls-default.txt
@@ -49,6 +49,31 @@
   Error message:     %s
   Location:          %s:%d
 #
+[not bound]
+PRTE could not bind a new process. The process will continue unbound.
+
+  Local host:        %s
+  Application name:  %s
+  Error message:     %s
+  Location:          %s:%d
+#
+[incorrectly bound]
+PRTE could not determine a new process's binding. It will continue bound
+to all available processors.
+
+  Local host:        %s
+  Application name:  %s
+  Location:          %s:%d
+#
+[memory not bound]
+PRTE could not bind memory for a new process. It will continue with CPU
+binding, but without memory binding. Performance may be degraded.
+
+  Local host:        %s
+  Application name:  %s
+  Error message:     %s
+  Location:          %s:%d
+#
 [iof setup failed]
 PRTE tried to launch a child process but the "IOF child setup"
 failed.  This should not happen.  Your job will now abort.
